<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! sense.guest.repaves ~ the guest rite: quiesce, verify, tear, stand, harvest

`lares mempalace repave` runs five idempotent steps (quiesce the holders, verify nothing holds the store and the worldline KG sits outside it, tear the guest tree, stand it again, harvest vanilla), so a rite that dies halfway re-runs from the top. Preview by default; `--confirm` enacts; `--keep-hooks` leaves the hooks paused afterward. It tears the guest alone.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ preview · enact

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`preview` params=`~ preview the rite`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`enact` params=`confirm/true ~ tear and stand the guest clean`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ confirm · keep-hooks

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`confirm` params=`~ enact the rite instead of previewing`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`keep-hooks` params=`~ leave the hooks paused afterward`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ local

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`local` params=`who/hand ~ tears and stands the guest palace on this host; this handler checks no ocap`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/refuses`>>

!! refuses ~ verb-error

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`verb-error` params=`cure/[[sense.guest.quiesces]] ~ a holder still holds the store, or the worldline KG sits inside it; quiesce first`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

